WEBVTT

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.220
I'm Jason, general manager at Formula
Fitness in Los Alamitos.

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:09.660
One of the first things we do with every
new member is put them on our InBody 580
scanner,

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.279
and there's a reason for that.

00:00:12.329 --> 00:00:17.198
Most people walk into a gym with a number
in their head, a goal weight.

00:00:17.248 --> 00:00:20.663
But weight alone doesn't tell you anything
useful.

00:00:20.713 --> 00:00:26.067
You could be losing muscle and gaining
fat, and the scale would still go down.

00:00:26.117 --> 00:00:28.700
That's not progress. That's a problem.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:34.257
The InBody 580 gives us a complete picture
in about 30 seconds.

00:00:34.307 --> 00:00:40.960
No pinching, no guessing. You step on,
grab the handle, and it measures
everything.

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:46.373
We get your exact body fat and fat free
mass so we know precisely where you're

00:00:46.423 --> 00:00:49.329
starting and exactly what needs to be
changed.

00:00:49.379 --> 00:00:54.727
We see your visceral fat area, that's the
fat around your internal organs, linked to

00:00:54.777 --> 00:00:56.976
diabetes, stroke and heart disease.

00:00:57.026 --> 00:01:02.310
That's the fat that actually matters. We
get a full segmental lean and fat analysis

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:08.152
meaning we can see exactly where the
muscle and fat lives on your body.

00:01:08.202 --> 00:01:10.283
Right arm, left leg, trunk.

00:01:10.333 --> 00:01:15.175
If there's an imbalance, we catch it and
we program around it.

00:01:15.225 --> 00:01:21.172
We also track phase angle, which is an
indicator of cellular health and cell

00:01:21.222 --> 00:01:25.670
membrane strength and your ECW to total
body water ratio.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:31.390
which can detect swelling, inflammation,
and fluid imbalances.

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:39.279
Also, your basal metabolic rate, which is
how many calories your body burns at rest.

00:01:39.329 --> 00:01:44.142
That's the starting point for any real
nutrition conversation.

00:01:44.192 --> 00:01:50.731
Now, some people ask, how does this
compare to the DEXA scan? A DEXA uses
radiation.

00:01:50.781 --> 00:01:53.320
The InBody 580 uses bioelectrical

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:54.108
impedance.

00:01:54.158 --> 00:01:59.700
It's completely non-invasive, takes about
30 seconds, and the accuracy is right

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:04.160
there with the DEXA for what we need in a
training environment.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:08.983
Plus, every scan syncs to the InBody app
on your phone.

00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:15.462
So you can see your results, track your
history, and watch your progress over
time.

00:02:15.512 --> 00:02:16.788
All in one place.

00:02:16.838 --> 00:02:22.486
You also get an InBody score, which gives
you one single number to track.

00:02:22.536 --> 00:02:24.750
Simple, easy, and motivating.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.792
At Formula Fitness, we don't guess, we
measure.

00:02:28.842 --> 00:02:34.206
We build your program around real data and
we track over time so you can actually

00:02:34.256 --> 00:02:35.476
see what's working.

00:02:35.526 --> 00:02:40.423
If you want to know where you really
stand, book your InBody scan with us.

00:02:40.473 --> 00:02:43.230
It's the smartest first step you can take.

